# =============================================================================
# PLACEHOLDER / TEMPLATE — Longhorn S3 backupstore credentials (Contabo Object
# Storage). Target namespace: longhorn-system.
#
# This is a *.template on purpose: it is NOT a real SealedSecret and is NOT
# synced by Argo. It documents the credential-wiring path WITHOUT committing
# real keys. The real sealed manifest (longhorn-s3-credentials.yaml) is produced
# offline by a human (steps below) and committed next to this file, where the
# `longhorn-backup` Argo Application (argocd/applications/longhorn-backup.yaml)
# syncs it into longhorn-system.
#
# ── Why this does NOT live under deploy/sealed-secrets/ ───────────────────────
# The `fuzeinfra-sealed-secrets` Argo app globs deploy/sealed-secrets/ with
# recurse and syncs into the `fuzeinfra` namespace, under the `fuzeinfra`
# AppProject — whose allowed destinations do NOT include longhorn-system. A
# longhorn-system SealedSecret placed there would make that whole app fail with
# InvalidSpecError and block every other FuzeInfra SealedSecret. So Longhorn's
# credential is owned by a separate `project: default` app instead.
#
# ── Why the keys are named AWS_* ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# "S3" is a protocol, not a provider. Longhorn (like the aws CLI and every S3
# SDK) hardcodes the field names AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY /
# AWS_ENDPOINTS regardless of who hosts the bucket. AWS_ENDPOINTS pointed at
# Contabo is exactly what sends the traffic to Contabo and nowhere near Amazon —
# no Amazon account, no AWS bill. This is the same Contabo Object Storage, same
# `fuzeinfra-backups` bucket, same account key pair the DB-dump CronJobs already
# use (docs/backups-and-blobs.md); only the key NAMES differ because Longhorn
# insists on these.
#
# ── How to produce/rotate the real file (offline, no cluster access) ──────────
# The S3 access key + secret are the SAME ACCOUNT-LEVEL pair that covers
# fuzeinfra-loki / fuzeinfra-backups / fuzeinfra-blobs. Fetch them from the
# Contabo API (NOT the panel), exactly as documented in
# deploy/sealed-secrets/loki-s3-credentials.yaml.template:
#   GET https://api.contabo.com/v1/users/<userId>/object-storages/credentials
#   (every api.contabo.com call needs an x-request-id header that is a valid UUID)
#
# Write each value to a throwaway file, then seal OFFLINE against FuzeInfra's
# published public cert into the longhorn-system namespace:
#
#   printf %s '<ACCESS_KEY_ID>'     > /tmp/lh_s3_key
#   printf %s '<SECRET_ACCESS_KEY>' > /tmp/lh_s3_secret
#   scripts/seal-secret.sh longhorn-system/longhorn-s3 \
#     AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=@/tmp/lh_s3_key \
#     AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=@/tmp/lh_s3_secret \
#     AWS_ENDPOINTS=https://eu2.contabostorage.com \
#     VIRTUAL_HOSTED_STYLE=false \
#     --out deploy/longhorn-system/longhorn-s3-credentials.yaml
#   shred -u /tmp/lh_s3_key /tmp/lh_s3_secret
#
# NOTES on the non-secret keys above:
#   * AWS_ENDPOINTS — REQUIRED. This is what redirects Longhorn to Contabo. It is
#     not a secret, but Longhorn only reads it from this Secret, so it is sealed
#     with the pair. Use the SAME endpoint the dumps use (eu2.contabostorage.com).
#   * VIRTUAL_HOSTED_STYLE=false — Contabo (like MinIO) needs PATH-STYLE
#     addressing; the DB dumps already set S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true for the same
#     reason (docs/backups-and-blobs.md §3).
#
# Commit ONLY the resulting encrypted longhorn-s3-credentials.yaml. NEVER accept
# the key values as a workflow input or chat paste — FuzeInfra job logs are
# public (CLAUDE.md).
#
# ── Shape of the REAL sealed output (for reference only) ─────────────────────
# apiVersion: bitnami.com/v1alpha1
# kind: SealedSecret
# metadata:
#   name: longhorn-s3
#   namespace: longhorn-system
# spec:
#   encryptedData:
#     AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID: <AgB...encrypted...>
#     AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: <AgB...encrypted...>
#     AWS_ENDPOINTS: <AgB...encrypted...>          # endpoint, sealed with the pair
#     VIRTUAL_HOSTED_STYLE: <AgB...encrypted...>   # "false"
#   template:
#     metadata:
#       name: longhorn-s3
#       namespace: longhorn-system
#     type: Opaque
# =============================================================================
